\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The normalized volume in odd dimension}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Fix an order on the #{n=2m+1} positive Euclidean directions.
Let #{S} be a nonzero finite-dimensional complex Hermitian space
with self-adjoint operators #{\varepsilon_j} satisfying
#{\varepsilon_i\varepsilon_j+\varepsilon_j\varepsilon_i
=2\delta_{ij}\bbI_S}. Their ordered product is the represented
pseudoscalar #{P=\psI=\varepsilon_1\cdots\varepsilon_n}.
It collects the ordered directions in one operator. The
\newvocab{normalized odd volume} and its sign spaces are
##{\omega=(-\ui)^m P,\qquad S_s=\ker(\omega-s\bbI_S)
\quad(s\in\{1,-1\}).}
A sign space may be zero. With a spectator fiber, all these
operators act as identity on that factor.}
